0
00:00:01,201 --> 00:00:04,137
♪♪♪

1
00:00:08,141 --> 00:00:10,143
Tyra: THE SEARCH FOR
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL

2
00:00:10,143 --> 00:00:12,212
STARTED WITH 14
STARRY-EYED GIRLS...

3
00:00:12,212 --> 00:00:14,414
All: (screaming)

4
00:00:14,414 --> 00:00:19,019
Tyra: AND THE COMPETITION
PROVED TO BE THE TOUGHEST YET.

5
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,420
MORE UNPREDICTABLE
PHOTO SHOOTS...

6
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,421
Jay: HARD TO BEAT.

7
00:00:21,421 --> 00:00:22,723
WHOA, WHOA!

8
00:00:22,723 --> 00:00:24,758
AMAZING MAKEUP.

9
00:00:24,758 --> 00:00:25,759
Tyra: MORE DRAMA...

10
00:00:25,759 --> 00:00:26,760
Ann: I DON'T FEEL--

11
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:27,961
Kristi: LET ME
OUT OF THE WAY.

12
00:00:27,961 --> 00:00:30,797
Toccara: OH, MY GOD!

13
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:32,332
(cries)

14
00:00:32,332 --> 00:00:34,301
Tyra: AND MORE
DIFFICULT CUTS.

15
00:00:34,301 --> 00:00:36,303
BUT THE COMPETITION
ENDS TONIGHT

16
00:00:36,303 --> 00:00:40,240
WHEN ONE GIRL WILL BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

17
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,342
WILL IT BE AMANDA,
WHO CAPTIVATED THE JUDGES

18
00:00:42,342 --> 00:00:45,312
FROM THE BEGINNING WITH HER
HYPNOTIC, ICE-BLUE EYES?

19
00:00:45,312 --> 00:00:46,713
Nolé: BEAUTIFUL EYES.

20
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:48,081
Tyra: HER EYES
ARE BREATHTAKING.

21
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:49,716
Jay: SO BEAUTIFUL.

22
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,785
Tyra: BUT NOBODY KNEW
THAT HER MOST STRIKING FEATURE

23
00:00:51,785 --> 00:00:53,887
WAS ALSO HER MOST TRAGIC.

24
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:57,324
Amanda: I'M LEGALLY BLIND.

25
00:00:57,324 --> 00:01:00,861
AND I'M GONNA BE ABOUT 30
WHEN I GO COMPLETELY BLIND.

26
00:01:00,861 --> 00:01:03,964
Tyra: AMANDA NEVER LET
HER DISABILITY HOLD HER BACK,

27
00:01:03,964 --> 00:01:07,401
DELIVERING GORGEOUS PHOTO
AFTER GORGEOUS PHOTO.

28
00:01:07,401 --> 00:01:09,803
BUT A TOP MODEL HAS TO LOOK
THE PART IN PERSON

29
00:01:09,803 --> 00:01:12,372
AS WELL AS ON FILM.

30
00:01:12,372 --> 00:01:17,044
TONIGHT, AMANDA HAS TO PROVE
HER STYLE CAN GO BEYOND QUIRKY.

31
00:01:17,044 --> 00:01:19,146
WILL IT BE EVA?

32
00:01:19,146 --> 00:01:21,715
DURING CASTING IN L.A.,
NOBODY SERVED IT QUITE LIKE

33
00:01:21,715 --> 00:01:23,450
LITTLE MISS EVA THE DIVA.

34
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:25,452
HOW DO YOU COMPARE YOURSELF
TO THE OTHER GIRLS OUT THERE?

35
00:01:25,452 --> 00:01:27,254
Eva: I DON'T COMPARE MYSELF
TO OTHER GIRLS.

36
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:28,689
I--I'M EVA.

37
00:01:28,689 --> 00:01:30,390
Tyra: 80% OF THE GIRLS
HAVE SOMETHING NEGATIVE

38
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:31,925
TO SAY ABOUT YOU.

39
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,794
BUT WHEN SHE FOUND OUT
HER ATTITUDE

40
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:37,264
WAS CAUSING CONTROVERSY,
HER TOUGH FACADE MELTED AWAY.

41
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:38,365
BUT YOU ARE
A SENSITIVE PERSON

42
00:01:38,365 --> 00:01:40,033
BECAUSE YOU'RE TEARING UP
RIGHT NOW,

43
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:42,936
AND THAT IS THE MOST BEAUTIFUL
PART OF YOU I'VE SEEN.

44
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:45,439
EVA'S STRUGGLE HAS BEEN MIXING
HER NATURAL SPUNK

45
00:01:45,439 --> 00:01:47,174
WITH A KIND
OF HIGH-FASHION GRACE

46
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:48,942
A TOP MODEL NEEDS.

47
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:51,845
TONIGHT, THE SHORTEST
OF THE BUNCH NEEDS TO DELIVER

48
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:54,448
A BIG PERFORMANCE TO PROVE
SHE CAN RISE ABOVE THE REST.

49
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:57,117
WILL IT BE YAYA,
THE IVY LEAGUE GRAD WHOSE ROAD

50
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:59,853
TO BECOME A TOP MODEL HAD
MORE THAN A FEW BUMPS ON IT?

51
00:01:59,853 --> 00:02:01,855
YAYA, WHAT IS YOUR
BIGGEST INSECURITY?

52
00:02:01,855 --> 00:02:03,857
Yaya: MY SKIN.

53
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:04,958
I NEVER KNOW
WHEN I'M GONNA WAKE UP

54
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,727
WITH MORE PIMPLES AND BUMPS.

55
00:02:06,727 --> 00:02:11,298
Tyra: I FOUND ONE OF THE BEST
DERMATOLOGISTS IN NEW YORK CITY.

56
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:13,700
WITH HER SKIN TROUBLE
BEHIND HER,

57
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:17,104
IT WAS YAYA'S NATURAL BEAUTY
THAT STARTED TO BREAK OUT.

58
00:02:17,104 --> 00:02:19,172
YAYA'S INTELLIGENCE
AND GRACEFUL PHYSIQUE

59
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:22,209
HAVE MADE HER STAND OUT
IN THE COMPETITION.

60
00:02:22,209 --> 00:02:25,045
BUT SOMETIMES
SHE SEEMS COLD IN PERSON.

61
00:02:25,045 --> 00:02:27,381
WILL YAYA PROVE THAT SHE CAN BE
RELATABLE AND REGAL

62
00:02:27,381 --> 00:02:29,383
AT THE SAME TIME?

63
00:02:29,383 --> 00:02:32,285
FROM L.A. TO NEW YORK,

64
00:02:32,285 --> 00:02:34,087
JAMAICA TO JAPAN,

65
00:02:34,087 --> 00:02:35,756
THESE THREE FINALISTS
HAVE BATTLED IT OUT.

66
00:02:35,756 --> 00:02:38,125
TONIGHT, THE SEASON FINALE.

67
00:02:38,125 --> 00:02:40,827
WHO WILL BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL?

68
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:44,031
♪♪♪

69
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:32,045
Eva: IT WAS 14,
AND THEN THERE WERE 3.

70
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:34,281
OH, MY GOD, THERE'S ONLY
A COUPLE OF ELIMINATIONS LEFT

71
00:03:34,281 --> 00:03:36,183
AND THEN SOMEONE'S GONNA BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL

72
00:03:36,183 --> 00:03:37,818
FOR REAL, FOR REAL.

73
00:03:37,818 --> 00:03:39,252
IT COULD BE ME.
IT COULD BE AMANDA.

74
00:03:39,252 --> 00:03:41,021
IT COULD BE YAYA.

75
00:03:41,021 --> 00:03:43,890
Yaya: THERE'S A THIRD
OF A CHANCE AT THIS POINT

76
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:46,526
THAT I COULD BE--
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

77
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:49,262
LIKE...

78
00:03:49,262 --> 00:03:51,398
Amanda: AFTER THE LAST
ELIMINATION

79
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:52,766
WHEN ANN HAD TO LEAVE,

80
00:03:52,766 --> 00:03:54,167
SHE ONLY HUGGED ME AND YAYA,

81
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:58,305
AND THEN WALKED RIGHT BY EVA
ON THE WAY OUT.

82
00:03:58,305 --> 00:04:00,507
Eva: BYE, 'NANA.

83
00:04:00,507 --> 00:04:03,210
FOR HER NOT EVEN TO SAY
GOOD-BYE, THAT WAS JUST--

84
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:05,278
IT WAS CRUSHING.

85
00:04:05,278 --> 00:04:07,147
Amanda: EVA HAD BEEN TREATING
ANN LIKE POO FOR, LIKE,

86
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:09,182
A REALLY LONG TIME.

87
00:04:09,182 --> 00:04:11,351
AND EVA'S JUST LIKE ME, ME, ME,
ME, ME, ME, ME, ME,

88
00:04:11,351 --> 00:04:13,386
ME, ME, ME, ME, ME, ME.

89
00:04:13,386 --> 00:04:14,788
Eva: I MEAN, THERE'S ALWAYS
CONSEQUENCES AND REPERCUSSIONS

90
00:04:14,788 --> 00:04:15,122
FOR THE THINGS YOU DO.

91
00:04:15,122 --> 00:04:16,223
Ann: WHEN I MET YOU,
I TOTALLY THOUGHT YOU WERE

92
00:04:16,223 --> 00:04:17,724
A DIFFERENT PERSON.

93
00:04:17,724 --> 00:04:19,659
I DON'T KNOW IF I LIKE
WHAT I SEE NOW.

94
00:04:19,659 --> 00:04:22,195
Eva: AFTER THE WHOLE THING
WENT DOWN WITH ANN,

95
00:04:22,195 --> 00:04:23,897
I UNDERSTAND
THE PART THAT I PLAYED.

96
00:04:23,897 --> 00:04:26,833
BUT I TAKE THIS AS A HUGE
LIFE-LEARNING EXPERIENCE.

97
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:28,835
BEING OFFENSIVE
AND BEING DEFENSIVE

98
00:04:28,835 --> 00:04:31,805
IS NOT SHOWING STRENGTH.

99
00:04:31,805 --> 00:04:34,241
I'M TRYING, AND I'M TRYING
TO BE THIS BETTER PERSON,

100
00:04:34,241 --> 00:04:36,309
BUT NO ONE'S EVEN SEEING IT.

101
00:04:36,309 --> 00:04:41,915
IT'S SO EASY TO JUST PUT A LABEL
ON SOMEBODY AND SHE'S THAT.

102
00:04:41,915 --> 00:04:45,585
Yaya: IF THERE WERE ANYTHING
THAT AMANDA AND I COULD DO

103
00:04:45,585 --> 00:04:48,889
TO MAKE EVA FEEL MORE INCLUDED
OR COMFORTABLE,

104
00:04:48,889 --> 00:04:50,190
I DON'T THINK WE WOULD.

105
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:53,293
TYRA MAIL.

106
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:57,931
"ACTRESSES HAVE RECENTLY
BEEN GRACING THE COVERS

107
00:04:57,931 --> 00:05:00,600
"OF ALL THE TOP MAGAZINES.

108
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,603
"BUT IT'S TIME FOR THEM
TO STEP ASIDE AND MAKE ROOM

109
00:05:03,603 --> 00:05:05,605
"FOR A REAL COVER GIRL.

110
00:05:05,605 --> 00:05:07,574
BE READY TO LEAVE
AT 8:15 IN THE MORNING."

111
00:05:09,843 --> 00:05:11,011
Yaya: I'M READY.

112
00:05:11,011 --> 00:05:14,214
Amanda: OKAY, WE READY.

113
00:05:18,251 --> 00:05:19,586
Yaya: THE NUMBER THREE--

114
00:05:19,586 --> 00:05:20,821
IT'S ALWAYS HARD
WITH THREE PEOPLE.

115
00:05:20,821 --> 00:05:23,590
I DON'T FEEL LIKE EXUDING
ANY EXTRA ENERGY

116
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:25,025
TO MAKE EVA FEEL INCLUDED.

117
00:05:25,025 --> 00:05:27,093
ALL MY ENERGY RIGHT NOW
REALLY NEEDS TO BE FOCUSED

118
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:29,296
ON WHY I'M HERE.

119
00:05:29,296 --> 00:05:30,897
Eva: AT THE LAST JUDGING,

120
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:32,699
TYRA SAYS, "THERE ARE FOUR
BEAUTIFUL GIRLS

121
00:05:32,699 --> 00:05:35,969
STANDING IN FRONT OF ME BUT"...

122
00:05:35,969 --> 00:05:38,305
Tyra: THE JUDGES CAN FIND
NOT ONE OF YOU

123
00:05:38,305 --> 00:05:41,074
THAT THEY THINK COULD BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

124
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:43,610
Eva: I THINK IT'S A GOOD THING,
BECAUSE IT JUST DOESN'T

125
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:45,178
GIVE US ANY SENSE OF IDENTITY
OR WHERE WE STAND

126
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:47,047
IN THIS COMPETITION.

127
00:05:47,047 --> 00:05:50,617
Amanda: NONE OF US
ARE STRONG IN EVERY ASPECT.

128
00:05:50,617 --> 00:05:52,352
RATHER THAN JUST LOOK LIKE
A MODEL IN MY PICTURES,

129
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:55,255
I NEED TO BE STRIKING
IN PERSON.

130
00:05:55,255 --> 00:05:57,157
Yaya: HEY.
Eva: GOOD MORNING.

131
00:05:57,157 --> 00:05:59,025
Jay: AND THEN
THERE WERE THREE.

132
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:00,894
WELL, TODAY
REALLY IS THE DAY.

133
00:06:00,894 --> 00:06:04,631
IT'S THE COVER GIRL PHOTO SHOOT
FOR WETSLICKS CRYSTALS.

134
00:06:04,631 --> 00:06:07,667
THIS IS A BRAND-NEW
MOISTURIZING LIP GLOSS

135
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:09,803
THAT COMES OUT THIS CHRISTMAS.

136
00:06:09,803 --> 00:06:12,572
SO THE WINNER
OF "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"

137
00:06:12,572 --> 00:06:15,976
IS GONNA HAVE THE AD
THAT WE SHOOT TODAY

138
00:06:15,976 --> 00:06:18,011
IN A NATIONAL MAGAZINE

139
00:06:18,011 --> 00:06:21,648
AND WILL KICK OFF
HER COVER GIRL CONTRACT.

140
00:06:21,648 --> 00:06:23,984
Yaya: IT'S SUCH AN IMPORTANT
SHOOT, BECAUSE IT'S ONE

141
00:06:23,984 --> 00:06:28,121
OF OUR VERY LAST CHANCES
TO SHOW UP THE OTHER TWO.

142
00:06:28,121 --> 00:06:31,358
Jay: WE'VE GOT THIS WATER POOL
HERE WITH THESE ZEN ROCKS.

143
00:06:31,358 --> 00:06:33,226
THIS IS A VERY
SPECIFIC LAYOUT.

144
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:35,262
THE LIP IS THE HERO TODAY.

145
00:06:35,262 --> 00:06:37,831
Amanda: I'M GONNA DO MY BEST
NO MATTER WHAT, YOU KNOW.

146
00:06:37,831 --> 00:06:39,199
HOPEFULLY MY BEST
WILL BE GOOD ENOUGH.

147
00:06:44,804 --> 00:06:47,207
Jay: THIS IS THE LIP GLOSS
WITH LASTING CRYSTAL SHINE.

148
00:06:47,207 --> 00:06:49,109
IT'S NOT STICKY,

149
00:06:49,109 --> 00:06:51,077
AND IT ACTS MORE LIKE A BALM
ON YOUR LIPS.

150
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:51,978
Amanda: HMM.

151
00:06:54,281 --> 00:06:56,950
Man: IT'S GOT THE CRYSTAL--
THE CRYSTAL FINISH IN IT.

152
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:58,818
Amanda: WHEN YOU'RE A LITTLE
GIRL THINKING ABOUT, LIKE,

153
00:06:58,818 --> 00:07:02,088
WANTING TO MODEL, YOU SAY,
"OH, I WANT TO DO THAT SOMEDAY."

154
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:06,960
BUT TO BE ON THE PRECIPICE
OF DOING IT IS JUST...

155
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,695
IT'S INSANE.

156
00:07:08,695 --> 00:07:10,597
Ryu: I'M RYU.
Amanda: LYU?

157
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:11,765
Ryu: RYU.
Amanda: AMANDA.

158
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:12,799
Jay: R-Y-U
IS HOW IT'S SPELLED.

159
00:07:12,799 --> 00:07:14,067
Amanda: OH, RYU.
Ryu: RYU.

160
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:17,337
Jay: THEY WANT YOU ON
THE FRONT-MOST PART OF THE ROCK,

161
00:07:17,337 --> 00:07:19,239
LIKE CLOSEST TO THE WATER EDGE
AS POSSIBLE.

162
00:07:19,239 --> 00:07:21,574
Amanda: OKAY.
Jay: NOW, AMANDA, SMILE.

163
00:07:21,574 --> 00:07:23,576
BUT IT'S THAT ENERGY,
THAT BRIGHTNESS,

164
00:07:23,576 --> 00:07:26,212
THAT APPROACHABLE ENERGY--
THAT'S WHAT WE NEED.

165
00:07:26,212 --> 00:07:28,214
EVEN THAT SMILE YOU'RE GIVING ME
RIGHT NOW WITH THOSE EYES.

166
00:07:28,214 --> 00:07:30,951
Ryu: OKAY, LET'S SHOOT.

167
00:07:35,121 --> 00:07:38,591
Amanda: I WAS REALLY TRYING
TO UTILIZE MY INNER JOY,

168
00:07:38,591 --> 00:07:43,096
YOU KNOW, MY REALLY STRONG
PERSONALITY AND MY APPRECIATION

169
00:07:43,096 --> 00:07:46,132
FOR BUNNY RABBITS AND FRANCE.

170
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:48,268
Jim: SHE'S GOT
CAMERA-READY SMILE.

171
00:07:48,268 --> 00:07:50,170
Jay: OH, MY GOSH,
SHE'S A COVER GIRL.

172
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:52,772
Amanda: I WAS SERVIN' UP
A PIPIN' HOT PLATE OF SMILE.

173
00:07:52,772 --> 00:07:54,307
Jay: AMANDA,
OUT OF 40 FRAMES,

174
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:56,309
YOU'VE GIVEN ME, LIKE,
36 PERFECT ONES.

175
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:58,244
AMANDA JUST GETS IT.

176
00:07:58,244 --> 00:08:00,280
SHE FEELS IT
INSIDE OF HERSELF.

177
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:03,650
AND SHE JUST EXUDES THE LOOK
THAT YOU ASK HER FOR.

178
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,185
Jim: GREAT, THAT'S IT.
Jay: THAT'S IT, RYU.

179
00:08:05,185 --> 00:08:06,953
Amanda: WHOO!

180
00:08:06,953 --> 00:08:09,856
Eva: I'M SO EXCITED
TO JUST MAKE IT THIS FAR.

181
00:08:09,856 --> 00:08:11,324
I AM ABOUT TO BE A STAR.

182
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,193
Jay: BE CAREFUL.

183
00:08:13,193 --> 00:08:14,961
AND YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO TRY
AND BRING YOUR OTHER ARM

184
00:08:14,961 --> 00:08:17,330
AND YOUR FACE CLOSER
TO THE EDGE OF THE WATER.

185
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,832
EXACTLY.

186
00:08:18,832 --> 00:08:20,734
THAT'S PRETTY.

187
00:08:20,734 --> 00:08:22,268
Eva: KNOWING THAT
IT'S ONLY THREE OF US,

188
00:08:22,268 --> 00:08:24,104
I HAVE NO ROOM FOR MESS-UPS.

189
00:08:24,104 --> 00:08:26,139
I CAN'T TWITCH WRONG,
LOOK WRONG.

190
00:08:26,139 --> 00:08:29,075
NOTHING CAN BE MESSED UP
RIGHT NOW.

191
00:08:29,075 --> 00:08:30,944
Jay: PRETTY.

192
00:08:30,944 --> 00:08:34,948
REMEMBER, I WANT TO KEEP THIS
FRIENDLY AND HAPPY.

193
00:08:34,948 --> 00:08:36,649
AND IT'S ABOUT AN INNER SMILE.

194
00:08:36,649 --> 00:08:38,251
CHIN UP A BIT.

195
00:08:38,251 --> 00:08:39,785
Amanda: I CAUGHT
A LITTLE GLIMPSE OF EVA

196
00:08:39,785 --> 00:08:42,688
HAVING A REALLY PRETTY FACE,
BUT I DIDN'T FEEL THE--

197
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,625
THE ENERGY COMING OUT.

198
00:08:45,625 --> 00:08:47,627
Jay: YES, I LIKE THAT.
I LIKE THAT.

199
00:08:47,627 --> 00:08:50,997
WHEN I THINK OF WHEN I MET EVA
AT THE CASTING,

200
00:08:50,997 --> 00:08:53,066
THERE WAS THIS TOUGH GIRL
WHO CAME OUT TO SERVE

201
00:08:53,066 --> 00:08:54,601
AND BE STRONG.

202
00:08:54,601 --> 00:08:56,603
AND I THINK, SLOWLY,
THROUGH THIS COMPETITION,

203
00:08:56,603 --> 00:08:57,904
SHE'S LET THAT WALL COME DOWN.

204
00:08:57,904 --> 00:08:59,105
Ryu: YEAH?
Jay: THAT'S IT, DONE.

205
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,642
Man: OKAY, MY DARLING,

206
00:09:02,642 --> 00:09:04,344
FINAL WETSLICK OF THE DAY.

207
00:09:04,344 --> 00:09:06,346
Yaya: EVERY TIME
I GET MY HAIR AND MAKEUP DONE,

208
00:09:06,346 --> 00:09:08,815
THEY TALK ABOUT THIS ELEGANT
THING, THIS REGAL THING.

209
00:09:08,815 --> 00:09:10,984
SO I WAS TRYING TO PULL
FROM ALL THESE DIFFERENT PLACES

210
00:09:10,984 --> 00:09:12,786
LIKE, HOW CAN I BE THAT--

211
00:09:12,786 --> 00:09:15,255
TEE-HEE, HA HA--
KIND OF PERSON?

212
00:09:15,255 --> 00:09:17,157
Jay: LOWER IS A LITTLE
BETTER, YAYA--IF YOU WANT

213
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:18,358
TO POSITION YOURSELF--

214
00:09:18,358 --> 00:09:21,795
BECAUSE THEN I GET MORE WATER.

215
00:09:21,795 --> 00:09:25,298
Yaya: I WAS FINDING SOME
MENTAL THING TO CONNECT WITH.

216
00:09:25,298 --> 00:09:28,234
YOU KNOW, I'M RECITING POETRY,
OR I'M SEEING LITTLE WAYS

217
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:32,305
IN WHICH MY EDUCATION'S
KEEPING ME POSITIVE

218
00:09:32,305 --> 00:09:34,040
THROUGH THIS EXPERIENCE.

219
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,042
Jay: KEEP YOUR ENERGY UP,
YAYA.

220
00:09:36,042 --> 00:09:38,311
REMEMBER, THINK
APPROACHABLE AND FRIENDLY.

221
00:09:38,311 --> 00:09:40,046
Jim: NICE.
Jay: PRETTY.

222
00:09:40,046 --> 00:09:42,115
OH, PRETTY.

223
00:09:42,115 --> 00:09:43,783
IN YAYA'S CASE,

224
00:09:43,783 --> 00:09:45,618
MATHU DID A BEAUTIFUL JOB
ON HER MAKEUP TODAY.

225
00:09:45,618 --> 00:09:47,253
SHE LOOKS FRESH,
NATURAL, AND BEAUTIFUL

226
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:48,655
WITHOUT EVEN RETOUCHING.

227
00:09:48,655 --> 00:09:50,857
Yaya: (trills) YEAH!

228
00:09:50,857 --> 00:09:51,858
Jay: LAST FRAME, THAT WAS IT.

229
00:09:51,858 --> 00:09:53,626
YOU DID SO GREAT.

230
00:09:56,129 --> 00:09:58,198
BEFORE TODAY, I DIDN'T THINK
ANY OF THE THREE GIRLS LEFT

231
00:09:58,198 --> 00:10:00,100
HAD IT IN THEM.

232
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,969
BUT TODAY, THE GIRLS JUST
ALL STEPPED UP TO THE PLATE.

233
00:10:02,969 --> 00:10:04,804
I THINK IT'S THE FACT
THAT THEY'RE REALIZING

234
00:10:04,804 --> 00:10:07,874
THAT THEY ARE SHOOTING
A REAL AD

235
00:10:07,874 --> 00:10:09,742
IF THEY WIN
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

236
00:10:19,686 --> 00:10:21,921
Eva: SO AFTER
THE PHOTO SHOOT,

237
00:10:21,921 --> 00:10:26,092
OUR CHALLENGE IS TO DO A GO-SEE
FOR NORIKO FUKUSHIMA.

238
00:10:26,092 --> 00:10:27,494
Jay: YO.

239
00:10:27,494 --> 00:10:28,962
Eva: HI.
Yaya: HELLO.

240
00:10:28,962 --> 00:10:30,630
Jay: SINCE YOU'VE BEEN HERE
IN TOKYO, YOU'VE LEARNED

241
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:33,933
ALL ABOUT TRADITIONAL FASHION
AND STREET-STYLE FASHION.

242
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:36,769
SO J AND I ARE HERE WITH NORIKO
TO TEACH YOU ABOUT

243
00:10:36,769 --> 00:10:38,872
CURRENT
READY-TO-WEAR FASHION.

244
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:42,041
Amanda: NORIKO IS A MAJOR
FASHION DESIGNER IN TOKYO.

245
00:10:44,878 --> 00:10:47,080
J.: AND NORIKO HAS BEEN

246
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,816
A FIXTURE ON THE FASHION SCENE
FOR THE PAST 20 YEARS.

247
00:10:49,816 --> 00:10:51,251
Jay: SO SHE KNOWS
WHAT SHE'S DOING.

248
00:10:51,251 --> 00:10:52,886
OKAY?

249
00:10:52,886 --> 00:10:54,654
Eva: I'M EXCITED
TO PUT SOME CLOTHES ON AND JUST

250
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,789
SEE SOMETHING DIFFERENT.

251
00:10:59,626 --> 00:11:00,860
Eva: I'M 5'7",

252
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:03,029
BUT I DON'T HAVE TO BE TALL
TO BE GREAT,

253
00:11:03,029 --> 00:11:05,231
TO KNOW THAT JUST ALL THE NORMS
CAN BE KNOCKED DOWN.

254
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,836
Noriko: (speaking Japanese)

255
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:13,907
Yaya: THE SKIRT
WAS KIND OF SEE-THROUGH.

256
00:11:13,907 --> 00:11:17,510
AND I DIDN'T WANT TO BE
DISRESPECTFUL, BUT IF THAT IDEA

257
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:20,947
HAD BEEN DONE IN THE STATES,
IT COULD'VE LOOKED VERY HOOCHIE.

258
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:25,051
J.: THIS IS HER VERSION
OF A WEDDING DRESS,

259
00:11:25,051 --> 00:11:26,653
A VERY MODERN WEDDING DRESS.

260
00:11:26,653 --> 00:11:28,821
Amanda: IT'S BEAUTIFUL.
IT'S A SHOW-STOPPER.

261
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:31,658
IT'S GORGEOUS.
IT WASN'T MY CUP OF TEA.

262
00:11:31,658 --> 00:11:34,160
I FELT KIND OF
OUT OF PLACE IN IT.

263
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,029
Jay: SO NOW YOU'VE BEEN
EVERYWHERE, FROM THE STREETS

264
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:38,765
TO TRADITIONAL TO HIGH FASHION.

265
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,569
Eva: TYRA MAIL!

266
00:11:42,569 --> 00:11:44,837
"TOMORROW YOU MEET
WITH THE JUDGES.

267
00:11:44,837 --> 00:11:47,173
"ONLY TWO OF YOU WILL CONTINUE
IN THE HOPES OF BECOMING

268
00:11:47,173 --> 00:11:48,975
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

269
00:11:48,975 --> 00:11:50,243
Amanda: WHAT?!

270
00:11:50,243 --> 00:11:52,779
TOP THREE WHO, WHAT?

271
00:11:52,779 --> 00:11:56,549
IT HASN'T SUNK IN YET
THAT I AM FINAL THREE,

272
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,084
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

273
00:11:58,084 --> 00:11:59,252
Eva: THIS IS CRAZY.

274
00:11:59,252 --> 00:12:01,788
I CANNOT BELIEVE
THAT I AM STILL HERE.

275
00:12:01,788 --> 00:12:04,190
THAT I AM SO FAR IN THIS
COMPETITION IS SO UNREAL TO ME.

276
00:12:04,190 --> 00:12:07,560
Yaya: I'M DEFINITELY
COMING TO PANEL WITH ANXIETY.

277
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,230
IT'S LIKE ALWAYS SO INTENSE.

278
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:13,132
AND IT'S JUST GONNA GET
EVEN MORE INTENSE.

279
00:12:20,006 --> 00:12:21,975
Tyra: WELCOME
TO THE JUDGING ROOM.

280
00:12:21,975 --> 00:12:25,111
TONIGHT IS A VERY SPECIAL
ELIMINATION.

281
00:12:25,111 --> 00:12:28,014
ONLY TWO OF YOU
WILL BE LEFT STANDING.

282
00:12:28,014 --> 00:12:31,618
AND THE TWO OF YOU WILL BE
COMPETING IN A FASHION SHOW

283
00:12:31,618 --> 00:12:35,054
FOR THE DESIGNER
NORIKO FUKUSHIMA.

284
00:12:35,054 --> 00:12:37,824
THE PERFORMANCE
IN THAT FASHION SHOW

285
00:12:37,824 --> 00:12:40,059
WILL HELP DETERMINE
WHO WILL BECOME

286
00:12:40,059 --> 00:12:41,961
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

287
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:45,131
OF COURSE, YOU ALL KNOW
WHAT OUR AMAZING PRIZES ARE,

288
00:12:45,131 --> 00:12:47,133
BUT LET ME
REFRESH YOUR MEMORIES--

289
00:12:47,133 --> 00:12:50,136
A CONTRACT WITH THE TOP
INTERNATIONAL MODELING AGENCY

290
00:12:50,136 --> 00:12:51,871
FORD MODELS,

291
00:12:51,871 --> 00:12:54,641
A SPREAD IN "ELLE" MAGAZINE,
WHICH WILL BE SHOT

292
00:12:54,641 --> 00:12:57,510
BY WORLD-RENOWNED PHOTOGRAPHER
GILLES BENSIMON,

293
00:12:57,510 --> 00:13:02,615
AND A $100,000 CONTRACT
WITH COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

294
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,784
AND, OF COURSE,
WE HAVE OUR JUDGES,

295
00:13:04,784 --> 00:13:07,954
WHICH YOU HAVE ALL COME
TO KNOW, LOVE, HATE.

296
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:10,590
FIRST, WE HAVE JANICE DICKINSON,
ONE OF THE WORLD'S FIRST

297
00:13:10,590 --> 00:13:12,725
SUPERMODELS EVER IN EXISTENCE.

298
00:13:12,725 --> 00:13:15,194
WE HAVE NIGEL BARKER,
NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER.

299
00:13:15,194 --> 00:13:18,598
NOLé MARIN, A PROMINENT
FASHION EDITOR AND STYLIST.

300
00:13:18,598 --> 00:13:20,166
AND, OF COURSE,
NORIKO FUKUSHIMA.

301
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:21,134
Noriko: KONNICHIWA.

302
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:23,603
All: KONNICHIWA.

303
00:13:23,603 --> 00:13:25,505
Tyra: AND MAO,
WHO WILL TRANSLATE FOR HER.

304
00:13:25,505 --> 00:13:27,473
YOU ALL SHOT A COVER GIRL AD.

305
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:30,076
THE WINNER OF AMERICA'S
NEXT TOP MODEL'S PHOTO

306
00:13:30,076 --> 00:13:35,248
WILL ACTUALLY BE A REAL AD
IN MAGAZINES,

307
00:13:35,248 --> 00:13:38,017
WHICH WILL BE THE START
OF HER COVER GIRL CONTRACT.

308
00:13:38,017 --> 00:13:39,652
SO, AMANDA.

309
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:40,653
Janice: JAPANDA.

310
00:13:40,653 --> 00:13:42,488
Tyra: HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

311
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:43,823
Nolé: OH.

312
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:44,824
Tyra: IT'S CUTE.

313
00:13:44,824 --> 00:13:45,825
Nigel: IT IS CUTE.

314
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:46,826
Nolé: THAT'S AMAZING.

315
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:47,827
Janice: IT'S LOVELY.

316
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:49,162
IT'S SCRUMPTIOUS.

317
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:51,064
IT'S ABSOLUTELY BEAUTIFUL.

318
00:13:51,064 --> 00:13:52,965
Nigel: YOU REALLY HAVE
CONNECTED WITH THE CAMERA,

319
00:13:52,965 --> 00:13:54,233
CONNECTED WITH THE AUDIENCE.

320
00:13:54,233 --> 00:13:55,668
MADE THEM WANT TO WEAR
COVER GIRL.

321
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:57,704
Amanda: I'M GONNA CRY.
Janice: CRY.

322
00:13:57,704 --> 00:13:59,505
CRYING IS GOOD.

323
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:02,542
Noriko: (speaking Japanese)

324
00:14:02,542 --> 00:14:04,811
Mao: YOUR HAIR
AND YOUR SKIN TONE AND YOUR EYES

325
00:14:04,811 --> 00:14:07,680
ARE SOMETHING JAPANESE PEOPLE
WOULD ADMIRE A LOT.

326
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,649
Tyra: AMANDA, WHAT DESIGNER
DO YOU THINK WOULD LET YOU

327
00:14:09,649 --> 00:14:10,950
WALK ON THE RUNWAY
WITH YOUR GLASSES?

328
00:14:10,950 --> 00:14:12,151
Amanda: IT DEPENDS.

329
00:14:12,151 --> 00:14:14,153
Nigel: YOUR GREATEST ASSET
IS YOUR EYES.

330
00:14:14,153 --> 00:14:15,955
Tyra: IT'S JUST NOT REALISTIC
FOR A GO-SEE

331
00:14:15,955 --> 00:14:18,591
AND FOR A REAL FASHION SHOW.

332
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:22,061
ALL RIGHTY, AMANDA, THANKS.

333
00:14:22,061 --> 00:14:24,130
UP NEXT IS YAYA.

334
00:14:24,130 --> 00:14:26,132
Nolé: WOW, YOU GIRLS
ARE DOING A GREAT JOB.

335
00:14:26,132 --> 00:14:27,133
Yaya: OH, MY GOD.

336
00:14:27,133 --> 00:14:28,701
THAT DOESN'T LOOK LIKE ME.

337
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:30,703
Nigel: YOU KNOW WHAT?
IT DOES LOOK LIKE YOU.

338
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:33,239
IT'S WHAT I'VE SEEN OUT OF YOU
RECENTLY, AND IT'S LOVELY

339
00:14:33,239 --> 00:14:34,707
TO SEE IT CAUGHT ON FILM.

340
00:14:34,707 --> 00:14:36,542
Tyra: I THINK
YOUR BONE STRUCTURE LOOKS

341
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:37,543
REALLY, REALLY BEAUTIFUL.

342
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,212
AND YOU DO LOOK
REALLY SWEET.

343
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,214
Nolé: YOU LOOK APPROACHABLE,
AND THAT'S WHAT WE WANT TO SEE.

344
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:43,049
Yaya: I WAS TRYING
NOT TO CONCENTRATE TOO MUCH,

345
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,818
BUT AT THE SAME TIME, YOU KNOW,
THINKING ABOUT, YOU KNOW,

346
00:14:45,818 --> 00:14:47,153
MY LITTLE BROTHER
MAKES ME LAUGH.

347
00:14:47,153 --> 00:14:49,989
Nigel: YOU WEREN'T THINKING
ABOUT THAT CONTRACT?

348
00:14:49,989 --> 00:14:51,991
ENOUGH TO PUT A SMILE
ON MOST PEOPLE'S FACES.

349
00:14:51,991 --> 00:14:53,226
Yaya: THAT, TOO.

350
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:54,994
Tyra: THANKS, YAYA.
NEXT IS EVA.

351
00:14:54,994 --> 00:14:56,996
Nigel: GOODNESS ME, YOU'RE
MAKING OUR JOBS DIFFICULT.

352
00:14:56,996 --> 00:14:59,165
Janice: CAN WE HAVE
THREE WINNERS TONIGHT, TYRA?

353
00:14:59,165 --> 00:15:00,800
Tyra: I WOULD LOVE TO.

354
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,034
Eva: I WAS THE ONE
THINKING ABOUT THE CONTRACT

355
00:15:02,034 --> 00:15:04,937
WHILE SHOOTING, AND THAT'S
WHAT KEPT ME MOTIVATED.

356
00:15:04,937 --> 00:15:06,973
KEPT ME SMILIN',
'CAUSE THAT'S WHAT I WANNA SEE

357
00:15:06,973 --> 00:15:08,808
WHEN I OPEN UP A MAGAZINE.

358
00:15:08,808 --> 00:15:11,744
Tyra: I THINK YOUR SKIN IS,
LIKE, AMAZING ON THIS PICTURE.

359
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:14,580
IT'S LIKE SO EVEN
AND SO SMOOTH.

360
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,948
Janice: SKIN LIKE HONEY.

361
00:15:15,948 --> 00:15:19,619
Noriko: (speaking Japanese)

362
00:15:19,619 --> 00:15:22,121
Mao: IT REALLY LOOKS LIKE
THE SMILE COMES FROM WITHIN,

363
00:15:22,121 --> 00:15:24,690
AND LOOKING AT THIS PICTURE
MAKES ME FEEL HAPPIER.

364
00:15:24,690 --> 00:15:26,526
Tyra: ALL RIGHTY, EVA.
THANKS.

365
00:15:29,061 --> 00:15:33,199
WELL, BEFORE I SEND YOU AWAY,
I JUST WANT TO APPLAUD

366
00:15:33,199 --> 00:15:34,801
ALL THREE OF YOU.

367
00:15:34,801 --> 00:15:36,035
'CAUSE Y'ALL
ARE THE THREE SHORTEST GIRLS

368
00:15:36,035 --> 00:15:37,236
IN THIS COMPETITION.
Eva: I SAID THAT!

369
00:15:37,236 --> 00:15:38,971
I SAID THAT.

370
00:15:38,971 --> 00:15:41,140
Tyra: NOW THERE ARE PEOPLE
IN THE FASHION WORLD

371
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:43,743
THAT MIGHT BE GAGGING, GOING,
"OH, THIS IS BLASPHEMOUS!"

372
00:15:43,743 --> 00:15:47,013
AND I THINK YOU ALL ARE GIVING
GIRLS HOPE THAT THEY'RE LIKE,

373
00:15:47,013 --> 00:15:50,516
"I AIN'T 5'9",
BUT IT JUST MAY BE OKAY."

374
00:15:50,516 --> 00:15:52,652
LAST WEEK WHEN I SAID
WE DIDN'T THINK THAT YOU GUYS

375
00:15:52,652 --> 00:15:54,821
WERE REALLY READY,
THOSE PICTURES

376
00:15:54,821 --> 00:15:56,622
PROVED US VERY WRONG.

377
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,057
THANKS, GUYS.

378
00:15:58,057 --> 00:16:00,159
Janice: SAYONARA.

379
00:16:02,595 --> 00:16:08,100
Tyra: NOW IT'S TIME TO DECIDE
WHICH ONE OF THESE THREE GIRLS

380
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,569
SHOULD GO HOME.

381
00:16:09,569 --> 00:16:10,770
Nolé: OH, GOSH.

382
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:11,871
Tyra: AMANDA.

383
00:16:11,871 --> 00:16:14,874
Noriko: (speaking Japanese)

384
00:16:14,874 --> 00:16:16,909
Mao: HER SKIN
IS EXTREMELY TRANSLUCENT

385
00:16:16,909 --> 00:16:18,578
AND HER HAIR IS BEAUTIFUL.

386
00:16:18,578 --> 00:16:20,780
Nolé: THE ICE QUEEN
HAS COMPLETELY MELTED AWAY

387
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:23,583
AND A BEAUTIFUL WOMAN
CAME OUT.

388
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:26,152
Tyra: THIS PHOTO OF HER
IS ABSOLUTELY BEAUTIFUL.

389
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:28,254
Nigel: AMANDA STILL NEEDS
TO WORK IN PERSON

390
00:16:28,254 --> 00:16:29,856
TO LOOK LIKE THIS.

391
00:16:29,856 --> 00:16:31,524
WHEN I'M LOOKING AT HER,
SHE'S OFF ON ONE LEG,

392
00:16:31,524 --> 00:16:33,125
AND SHE SEEMS LIKE HER BODY'S
SLIGHTLY OFF ON AN ANGLE

393
00:16:33,125 --> 00:16:33,726
ALL THE TIME.

394
00:16:33,726 --> 00:16:35,862
Janice: AMANDA,
IN THIS PHOTOGRAPH, NAILS IT--

395
00:16:35,862 --> 00:16:37,430
HANDS DOWN, BAR NONE.

396
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:38,631
Tyra: EVA.

397
00:16:38,631 --> 00:16:40,766
Nigel: SHE
IS THIS LITTLE TOMBOY.

398
00:16:40,766 --> 00:16:42,435
SHE'S NOT THE GIRL THAT YOU
NECESSARILY THINK IS GONNA

399
00:16:42,435 --> 00:16:43,803
PULL OUT A PICTURE
LIKE THIS.

400
00:16:43,803 --> 00:16:46,873
THIS IS A GREAT, BEAUTIFUL,
WARM PICTURE.

401
00:16:46,873 --> 00:16:48,941
Nolé: THIS IS THE GIRL
THAT EVERY GIRL IN AMERICA

402
00:16:48,941 --> 00:16:50,676
WANTS TO KNOW
AND WANTS TO BE.

403
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:51,677
SHE'S UNIVERSAL.

404
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,880
Janice: EVA HAS COME
LIGHT-YEARS.

405
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:57,884
SHE'S LEAPT, AND SHE'S LEARNED,
BUT I STILL WANT TO SEE CHIC.

406
00:16:57,884 --> 00:17:00,586
AND I DON'T GET THE ESSENCE
OF CHIC ABOUT HER.

407
00:17:00,586 --> 00:17:01,621
Tyra: YAYA.

408
00:17:01,621 --> 00:17:03,456
Nolé: SHE'S
ABSOLUTELY BEAUTIFUL.

409
00:17:03,456 --> 00:17:05,424
YAYA HAS INCREDIBLE
BONE STRUCTURE.

410
00:17:05,424 --> 00:17:07,059
Nigel: YAYA IS REALLY
ONE OF THE MOST BEAUTIFUL GIRLS

411
00:17:07,059 --> 00:17:08,594
I THINK WE'VE HAD.

412
00:17:08,594 --> 00:17:10,029
Nolé: I AGREE.
Nigel: SHE'S STUNNING.

413
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:11,797
AND WHEN SHE STANDS
IN FRONT OF YOU, SHE'S ELEGANT.

414
00:17:11,797 --> 00:17:13,398
SHE'S REGAL.

415
00:17:13,398 --> 00:17:15,434
BUT THOSE THINGS ARE ALSO HER
DOWN POINTS SOMETIMES.

416
00:17:15,434 --> 00:17:17,002
SHE DEFINITELY HAS THAT SLIGHT

417
00:17:17,002 --> 00:17:18,804
ARROGANT SORT OF SNOBBISH THING
ABOUT HER.

418
00:17:18,804 --> 00:17:19,805
Janice: THAT'S YOUR OPINION.

419
00:17:19,805 --> 00:17:20,973
Nigel: WELL,
IT IS MY OPINION.

420
00:17:20,973 --> 00:17:22,407
ISN'T THAT WHAT THIS IS ABOUT?

421
00:17:22,407 --> 00:17:24,810
Janice: SO THAT DETERS
THE WAY SHE WALKS,

422
00:17:24,810 --> 00:17:27,847
THE WAY SHE LOOKS,
THAT SHE HAS AN AIR ABOUT HER?

423
00:17:27,847 --> 00:17:30,616
Nigel: PHOTOGRAPHICALLY,
IT'S HARD TO CRITICIZE HER.

424
00:17:30,616 --> 00:17:32,752
SHE'S HAD CONSISTENT
BEAUTIFUL PICTURES,

425
00:17:32,752 --> 00:17:34,420
AS HAS AMANDA.

426
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:36,422
AS HAVE ALL THREE GIRLS,
I THINK, BUT, UM--

427
00:17:36,422 --> 00:17:38,891
Janice: THIS PICTURE
CROSSES ALL BORDERS.

428
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:41,394
I THINK YAYA'S GOT
THE COVER GIRL LOOK.

429
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:43,129
Tyra: THIS IS, LIKE,
THE HARDEST JUDGING I'VE EVER--

430
00:17:43,129 --> 00:17:44,730
Janice: IT'S SO HARD.

431
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,032
Nigel: ALL THESE GIRLS CAN
DO PRETTY WELL PHOTOGRAPHICALLY.

432
00:17:46,032 --> 00:17:49,635
SO IT'S A DIFFICULT ONE
FOR ME TO DECIDE ON.

433
00:17:49,635 --> 00:17:51,971
Tyra: I'M SHAKING, YOU GUYS.

434
00:18:02,648 --> 00:18:06,385
Tyra: I HAVE THREE LOVELY
LADIES STANDING IN FRONT OF ME,

435
00:18:06,385 --> 00:18:11,791
BUT I ONLY HAVE TWO PHOTOS
IN MY HANDS.

436
00:18:11,791 --> 00:18:15,361
THESE TWO PHOTOS REPRESENT
THE TWO FINALISTS.

437
00:18:15,361 --> 00:18:19,665
THESE TWO FINALISTS WILL COMPETE
IN A NORIKO FUKUSHIMA

438
00:18:19,665 --> 00:18:21,968
FASHION SHOW
AND WILL WALK

439
00:18:21,968 --> 00:18:25,905
AND SASHAY TO THE DEATH
TO SEE WHO CAN BE

440
00:18:25,905 --> 00:18:27,773
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

441
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:30,009
THE FIRST NAME
THAT I'M GOING TO CALL...

442
00:18:33,479 --> 00:18:35,081
Tyra: YAYA.

443
00:18:35,081 --> 00:18:38,818
Yaya: (sighs)

444
00:18:38,818 --> 00:18:40,353
Tyra: YAYA, YOU WALKED

445
00:18:40,353 --> 00:18:43,656
IN HERE A BEAUTIFUL GIRL
WITH GREAT STATURE

446
00:18:43,656 --> 00:18:45,591
BUT A LITTLE BIT
TOO MUCH STATURE,

447
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:47,760
BECAUSE YOU WERE THE DANCER.

448
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:50,663
BUT THESE JUDGES HONED THAT IN.

449
00:18:50,663 --> 00:18:52,064
NOW YOU'RE A MODEL.

450
00:18:52,064 --> 00:18:55,701
YAYA, YOU ARE A FINALIST.

451
00:18:55,701 --> 00:18:59,405
THERE IS A 50/50 CHANCE
THAT YOU WILL BE

452
00:18:59,405 --> 00:19:01,440
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

453
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,943
Yaya: (sighs)
Tyra: CONGRATULATIONS.

454
00:19:03,943 --> 00:19:05,544
Yaya: THANK YOU.

455
00:19:10,316 --> 00:19:15,688
Tyra: WILL EVA AND AMANDA
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

456
00:19:15,688 --> 00:19:18,057
I ONLY HAVE ONE PHOTO
IN MY HANDS.

457
00:19:18,057 --> 00:19:21,460
AND THIS ONE PHOTO REPRESENTS
THE GIRL THAT WILL CONTINUE ON

458
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:25,531
IN THE RUNNING TOWARDS BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

459
00:19:25,531 --> 00:19:27,233
I WILL ONLY CALL ONE NAME.

460
00:19:27,233 --> 00:19:30,870
THE GIRL THAT I DO NOT CALL
MUST IMMEDIATELY RETURN

461
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:35,374
TO YOUR JAPANESE HOMESTAY,
PACK YOUR BELONGINGS AND LEAVE.

462
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:42,648
YOU TWO ARE A VERY INTERESTING
LITTLE DUO HERE.

463
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:46,952
YOU GUYS BOTH HAVE
WHAT THE OTHER NEEDS.

464
00:19:46,952 --> 00:19:53,693
AMANDA, YOU HAVE EDGY, FIERCE,
HIGH-FASHION AMAZINGNESS.

465
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:57,930
EVA, YOU HAVE APPROACHABLE,
RELATABLE,

466
00:19:57,930 --> 00:20:01,100
BUT TO BE A TOP MODEL,
YOU HAVE TO HAVE BOTH.

467
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:05,604
SO YOU GUYS
ARE INCOMPLETE PACKAGES.

468
00:20:05,604 --> 00:20:08,741
THERE IS ONE OF YOU
THAT THE JUDGES THINK

469
00:20:08,741 --> 00:20:10,776
IN THIS SHORT TIME
MIGHT BE ABLE

470
00:20:10,776 --> 00:20:12,144
TO PULL IT TOGETHER.

471
00:20:18,150 --> 00:20:18,951
Tyra: EVA.

472
00:20:18,951 --> 00:20:20,686
Eva: OH!

473
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,091
Tyra: CONGRATULATIONS.

474
00:20:25,091 --> 00:20:26,992
YOU'RE A FINALIST.

475
00:20:26,992 --> 00:20:28,794
Amanda: THANKS AGAIN.

476
00:20:28,794 --> 00:20:33,899
Tyra: YOU THOUGHT YOU WERE
GOIN' HOME TONIGHT, DIDN'T YOU?

477
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,736
Janice: (sighs)

478
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:47,179
Janice: LOVE YOU.

479
00:20:47,179 --> 00:20:52,918
Amanda: (speaking Japanese)
I'M PRETTY SURPRISED.

480
00:20:52,918 --> 00:20:55,921
I THOUGHT I WAS GONNA BE
FINAL TWO.

481
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:59,158
I WANTED TO WIN SO I COULD GET
THAT $100,000 CONTRACT

482
00:20:59,158 --> 00:21:01,393
AND BUY A HOUSE.

483
00:21:01,393 --> 00:21:04,063
AT LEAST I GOT TO DO THIS.

484
00:21:04,063 --> 00:21:08,634
I WANT TO INSPIRE PEOPLE
THAT HAVE DISABILITIES

485
00:21:08,634 --> 00:21:12,671
OR, YOU KNOW, SHORTCOMINGS
TO JUST, LIKE, WORK THROUGH IT

486
00:21:12,671 --> 00:21:16,142
AND TO FIND JOY IN EVERYTHING.

487
00:21:27,653 --> 00:21:30,456
Eva: WELL, AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL IS, LIKE, ONE OF US.

488
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:34,326
EITHER THE TOMBOY
OR THE AFROCENTRIC ONE

489
00:21:34,326 --> 00:21:36,695
IS GONNA BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

490
00:21:36,695 --> 00:21:38,764
YAYA AND I ARE FINAL TWO NOW.

491
00:21:38,764 --> 00:21:41,634
NEVER IN A MILLION YEARS
DID WE THINK THAT WE WOULD BE

492
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:43,169
THE LAST TWO.

493
00:21:43,169 --> 00:21:45,571
DID YOU NOTICE THAT WE ARE
EACH OTHERS COMPETITION?

494
00:21:45,571 --> 00:21:48,274
IT JUST BLOWS ME THAT IT'S STILL
TWO BLACK GIRLS HERE.

495
00:21:48,274 --> 00:21:50,042
WE ARE EACH OTHERS COMPETITION.

496
00:21:50,042 --> 00:21:53,412
Yaya: (laughs)
EVA AND I, UP UNTIL THIS POINT,

497
00:21:53,412 --> 00:21:56,315
HAVEN'T FELT COMFORTABLE
AROUND EACH OTHER.

498
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:58,717
WE JUST DIDN'T FIND
THAT CONNECTION.

499
00:21:58,717 --> 00:22:01,120
AND SO NOW IT'S JUST HER AND ME.

500
00:22:01,120 --> 00:22:02,788
WE JUST LET OUR GUARDS DOWN.

501
00:22:02,788 --> 00:22:04,790
Eva: WHAT MADE ME DIFFERENT
THAN THE OTHER GIRL

502
00:22:04,790 --> 00:22:08,427
SITTING RIGHT NEXT TO ME
THAT IS EQUALLY AS BEAUTIFUL?

503
00:22:08,427 --> 00:22:10,162
AND TALLER.

504
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,463
YOU KNOW WHAT I'M SAYIN'?

505
00:22:11,463 --> 00:22:15,167
STRAIGHTER TEETH
AND GLOWIER SKIN.

506
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,168
Yaya: HELLO.

507
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,436
CLEARER SKIN.

508
00:22:17,436 --> 00:22:20,506
NESTLE CRUNCH BAR
AND, "YEAH, SHE'S CUTE, BUT..."

509
00:22:20,506 --> 00:22:23,409
Eva: WHAT I'M LEARNING
ABOUT YAYA IS THAT SHE

510
00:22:23,409 --> 00:22:27,246
HAS HER DEFENSES UP,
BUT THAT THERE IS A SWEET PERSON

511
00:22:27,246 --> 00:22:28,647
UNDERNEATH ALL OF THAT.

512
00:22:28,647 --> 00:22:32,084
IN THIS WHOLE TIME,
I WAS UNABLE TO SEE THAT.

513
00:22:32,084 --> 00:22:34,320
Yaya: THERE'S NO ONE ELSE
THAT WALKED INTO L.A. LIKE...

514
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,188
(snaps fingers)
I GOT IT.

515
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:37,556
NOBODY WALKED IN LIKE THAT.

516
00:22:37,556 --> 00:22:40,459
IT JUST MAKES ME HAPPY
THAT THE PERSON THAT'S GONNA WIN

517
00:22:40,459 --> 00:22:43,729
IS GOING TO BE A BLACK WOMAN
WHO HAS FLAWS,

518
00:22:43,729 --> 00:22:47,666
WHOSE HEAD IS ON HER SHOULDERS
AND WHO IS A POSITIVE PERSON.

519
00:22:47,666 --> 00:22:49,301
Eva: THIS IS SO RETARDED.

520
00:22:49,301 --> 00:22:53,505
Yaya: IT'S SO REFRESHING
TO BE ABLE TO FINALLY SEE

521
00:22:53,505 --> 00:22:56,442
A LITTLE BIT OF HER
FOR WHO SHE IS, AND I'M LIKE,

522
00:22:56,442 --> 00:22:58,377
"WHY COULDN'T IT HAVE BEEN
THIS WAY THE WHOLE TIME?"

523
00:23:01,413 --> 00:23:03,349
Eva: I WAKE UP
IN THE MORNING, AND IT'S TIME

524
00:23:03,349 --> 00:23:07,853
FOR OUR ONE-ON-ONE WITH TYRA
BEFORE OUR FINAL CHALLENGE.

525
00:23:10,422 --> 00:23:13,158
Tyra: SO HAVE A SEAT,
MISS EVA.

526
00:23:13,158 --> 00:23:15,094
SO HOW ARE YOU FEELING
RIGHT NOW?

527
00:23:15,094 --> 00:23:17,796
Eva: NEVER IN A MILLION YEARS
COULD I HAVE IMAGINED--

528
00:23:17,796 --> 00:23:20,933
I MEAN, MODELING,
BECOMING A SUPERMODEL IS JUST--

529
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:23,302
IT'S JUST A DREAM,
NOTHING THAT I EVER THOUGHT

530
00:23:23,302 --> 00:23:24,970
WAS OBTAINABLE.

531
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:26,972
YOU KNOW, IT'S TWO PEOPLE LEFT,
AND THEY'RE BLACK.

532
00:23:26,972 --> 00:23:29,108
GET THAT.
LIKE, WHAT?

533
00:23:29,108 --> 00:23:31,610
Tyra: IT'S NOT ABOUT US
THINKING, "OH, A BLACK GIRL

534
00:23:31,610 --> 00:23:33,279
NEEDS TO WIN THIS YEAR."

535
00:23:33,279 --> 00:23:36,582
IT'S JUST THE TWO BEST
WERE BLACK GIRLS.

536
00:23:36,582 --> 00:23:38,584
I KNOW YOU TOLD ME
THAT YOU WERE KIND OF ALIENATED,

537
00:23:38,584 --> 00:23:40,185
YOU KNOW, FROM THE OTHER GIRLS.

538
00:23:40,185 --> 00:23:42,321
HOW DO YOU THINK IT'S GONNA BE
NOW THAT THERE'S TWO?

539
00:23:42,321 --> 00:23:44,189
Eva: IT'S WEIRD,
BECAUSE YAYA AND I HAVE NEVER

540
00:23:44,189 --> 00:23:47,092
TAKEN IT UPON OURSELVES
TO GET TO KNOW EACH OTHER.

541
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,128
BUT WE WENT THROUGH THIS
TOGETHER,

542
00:23:49,128 --> 00:23:50,296
AND WE BOTH KNOW.

543
00:23:50,296 --> 00:23:54,934
AND TO BE ENEMIES HERE AND NOW
IS SO POINTLESS.

544
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:56,902
Tyra: WAS THERE ANYTHING
YOU WANTED TO ASK ME?

545
00:23:56,902 --> 00:23:58,537
Eva: WHAT DO YOU SEE IN ME
THAT SHOWS YOU

546
00:23:58,537 --> 00:23:59,872
THAT I HAVE SO MUCH POTENTIAL?

547
00:23:59,872 --> 00:24:03,309
Tyra: A GIRL
THAT IS VERY TROUBLED

548
00:24:03,309 --> 00:24:07,246
BUT IS DEALING WITH THAT
AND IS TRYING TO BE BETTER.

549
00:24:07,246 --> 00:24:10,749
SO IT'S NOT ABOUT PERFECTION,
BUT IT'S ABOUT STRIVING

550
00:24:10,749 --> 00:24:12,718
TO IMPROVE OURSELVES.

551
00:24:12,718 --> 00:24:14,620
Eva: OH, I'M ABOUT TO CRY.

552
00:24:14,620 --> 00:24:18,991
UM, IT IS SO AMAZING,
BECAUSE IF I LOOK AT MY PAST,

553
00:24:18,991 --> 00:24:21,593
WHAT I'VE GONE THROUGH,
TO TRY TO PREDICT MY FUTURE

554
00:24:21,593 --> 00:24:24,129
AND SAY, "IN FIVE YEARS
WHERE WOULD I BE?"

555
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:25,597
ALL I WANTED
WAS SOMEWHERE TO SLEEP

556
00:24:25,597 --> 00:24:28,100
OR SOMEONE TO HOLD ME
OR SOMEONE TO LOVE ME.

557
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:32,738
AND I HAVE ADMIRED
SO MANY PEOPLE IN MY TIME.

558
00:24:32,738 --> 00:24:34,940
I COULD POSSIBLY BE SOMEONE
THAT EVERYBODY ADMIRES,

559
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:37,042
AND WHAT?!

560
00:24:37,042 --> 00:24:40,012
YOU KNOW, THERE'S NEVER
A TESTIMONY WITHOUT A TEST.

561
00:24:40,012 --> 00:24:43,182
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

562
00:24:43,182 --> 00:24:44,183
Tyra: HELLO.

563
00:24:44,183 --> 00:24:45,651
Yaya: HI, TYRA.

564
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:46,652
HOW ARE YOU?

565
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:47,653
Tyra: I'M HYPERVENTILATING.

566
00:24:47,653 --> 00:24:49,054
Yaya: I AM, MY GOSH.

567
00:24:49,054 --> 00:24:52,024
I'M JUST COMING BACK DOWN
FROM, LIKE, TO REALITY.

568
00:24:52,024 --> 00:24:53,892
I WASN'T EXPECTING YOU
TO CALL ME FIRST

569
00:24:53,892 --> 00:24:55,828
OR AT ALL, I DON'T KNOW,
IT'S JUST--

570
00:24:55,828 --> 00:24:57,329
Tyra: WHY WERE YOU
QUESTIONING YOUR BELONGING HERE?

571
00:24:57,329 --> 00:25:00,966
Yaya: BECAUSE
I'M USUALLY VERY--

572
00:25:00,966 --> 00:25:02,935
AND I DON'T LIKE THE WORD...

573
00:25:02,935 --> 00:25:06,939
(whispers) AFROCENTRIC,
BUT IT'S JUST VERY NATURAL

574
00:25:06,939 --> 00:25:11,076
FOR ME TO WANT TO EXPRESS THAT,
YOU KNOW, AND TO WANT

575
00:25:11,076 --> 00:25:13,112
TO BE PROUD.

576
00:25:13,112 --> 00:25:16,582
I NEVER WANTED TO, YOU KNOW,
FILL THIS MOLD THAT I FELT

577
00:25:16,582 --> 00:25:18,650
THAT EVERYONE ELSE WAS FILLING.

578
00:25:18,650 --> 00:25:20,319
Tyra: YOU KNOW,
YEAH, I'LL WEAR A HAIR WEAVE,

579
00:25:20,319 --> 00:25:22,955
BUT I'M STILL A BLACK WOMAN.

580
00:25:22,955 --> 00:25:24,957
AND I'M STILL
REPRESENTING BEAUTY TO PEOPLE

581
00:25:24,957 --> 00:25:27,659
THAT NEVER REALLY THOUGHT
BLACK WOMEN WERE BEAUTIFUL.

582
00:25:27,659 --> 00:25:31,764
THERE'S A WAY TO MAKE PEOPLE
LOOK AT YAYA AND SAY,

583
00:25:31,764 --> 00:25:35,000
"OH, MY GOSH,
YOU HAVE THE KENTE CLOTH

584
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:37,136
"AND IT'S THIS AND IT'S THAT,
BUT I'M A WHITE FROM ALABAMA,

585
00:25:37,136 --> 00:25:39,238
"AND I STILL LIKE HER.

586
00:25:39,238 --> 00:25:41,073
I'M NOT INTIMIDATED BY HER."

587
00:25:41,073 --> 00:25:43,976
DO YOU UNDERSTAND ABOUT STILL
HOLDING ONTO WHO YOU ARE

588
00:25:43,976 --> 00:25:47,713
BUT BEING ABLE TO RELATE
TO A LOT OF DIFFERENT PEOPLE?

589
00:25:52,317 --> 00:25:54,186
Eva: GET READY, BACKSTAGE.

590
00:25:54,186 --> 00:25:56,088
Yaya: OOH.

591
00:25:56,088 --> 00:25:58,123
Eva: I'M ABOUT TO COME SHOW
YOU SOME BLACK BOOTY.

592
00:25:58,123 --> 00:25:59,691
TODAY'S THE DAY.

593
00:25:59,691 --> 00:26:02,094
WE HAVIN' A FASHION SHOW,
AND I CAN WALK.

594
00:26:02,094 --> 00:26:04,963
SO I SO WANNA WIN THIS,
AND I'M GONNA SHOW IT

595
00:26:04,963 --> 00:26:06,298
IN EVERY STEP OF THE WAY TODAY.

596
00:26:06,298 --> 00:26:07,900
I'M GONNA KILL IT.

597
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:08,967
Jay: YAYA, EVA, HOW ARE YOU?

598
00:26:08,967 --> 00:26:10,135
Eva: HI.

599
00:26:10,135 --> 00:26:12,204
Jay: THE TWO GIRLS
IN THE HOUSE.

600
00:26:12,204 --> 00:26:15,541
Yaya: I DEFINITELY HAVE
THOSE BUTTERFLIES IN MY STOMACH

601
00:26:15,541 --> 00:26:18,043
GOIN' ON, AND I FEEL
THE SAME WAY I DID

602
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:20,179
WHEN I WALKED ACROSS THE STAGE
AND GOT MY DIPLOMA.

603
00:26:20,179 --> 00:26:22,181
AND I KNOW I HAVEN'T WON YET,
BUT...

604
00:26:22,181 --> 00:26:25,717
(sighs)
ALMOST.

605
00:26:25,717 --> 00:26:28,253
Both: (scream)
Jay: SO, YEAH, I KNOW, RIGHT?

606
00:26:28,253 --> 00:26:29,888
EXCITING.

607
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:32,157
SO THIS IS NOT A SHOW
FOR YOU TWO.

608
00:26:32,157 --> 00:26:34,693
IT'S A REAL
FASHION SHOW FOR NORIKO.

609
00:26:34,693 --> 00:26:37,596
Yaya: THIS IS NOT AN EVENT
FOR THE TOP TWO OF

610
00:26:37,596 --> 00:26:38,664
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

611
00:26:38,664 --> 00:26:40,999
THIS IS NOT ABOUT US.

612
00:26:40,999 --> 00:26:43,936
OOH.

613
00:26:43,936 --> 00:26:46,038
Eva: OH, LOOK AT THE STAGE.

614
00:26:46,038 --> 00:26:48,674
LOOK, PEOPLE ARE GONNA BE
SITTING IN THE MIDDLE HERE.

615
00:26:48,674 --> 00:26:51,310
Yaya: WE NEVER THOUGHT ABOUT
THAT KIND OF RUNWAY.

616
00:26:51,310 --> 00:26:53,612
WE'VE ALWAYS BEEN
BACK AND FORTH, YOU KNOW,

617
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:55,314
ON THIS VERY LINEAR RUNWAY.

618
00:26:55,314 --> 00:26:59,118
THOSE 45 DEGREE, LIKE, HOW DO
I KNOW TO STEP WITH THIS FOOT

619
00:26:59,118 --> 00:27:02,121
OR THE ONE OVER OR, YOU KNOW,
DO I LOOK HERE AND THEN GO?

620
00:27:02,121 --> 00:27:05,557
Jay: WE'RE GOING FOR A VERY
JAPANESE ZEN-STYLE SHOW.

621
00:27:05,557 --> 00:27:10,095
THEREFORE THE WALK
IS A VERY SOMBER, VERY SLOW.

622
00:27:10,095 --> 00:27:11,730
Eva: WHAT?!

623
00:27:11,730 --> 00:27:13,632
WHAT WE'VE BEEN TAUGHT HERE
SO FAR IS HOW TO BE FIERCE,

624
00:27:13,632 --> 00:27:15,033
JUST GIVE IT AND BRING IT.

625
00:27:15,033 --> 00:27:16,902
I'M DEFINITELY NERVOUS.

626
00:27:16,902 --> 00:27:19,705
Jay: AND YOU JUST FOLLOW
THE PATTERN OF THE RUNWAY.

627
00:27:19,705 --> 00:27:21,540
Yaya: SEEING
THESE OTHER MODELS,

628
00:27:21,540 --> 00:27:22,908
IT WAS REALLY COMFORTING.

629
00:27:22,908 --> 00:27:24,910
I JUST FELT LIKE,
"OH, I CAN DO THIS."

630
00:27:42,161 --> 00:27:43,962
Yaya: THIS IS THE END,
AND THIS IS THE FASHION SHOW.

631
00:27:43,962 --> 00:27:46,131
AND OUR JOB IS TO STEP UP
TO THE PLATE AND ACT

632
00:27:46,131 --> 00:27:48,066
LIKE WE DO THIS ALL THE TIME.

633
00:27:48,066 --> 00:27:50,736
Eva: THIS IS DEFINITELY
EVERYTHING I'VE EVER DREAMT OF,

634
00:27:50,736 --> 00:27:53,739
FROM GETTING MY MAKEUP DONE
TO GETTING MY HAIR DONE.

635
00:27:53,739 --> 00:27:55,140
OH, MY GOD.

636
00:27:55,140 --> 00:27:56,775
IT'S LIKE GRADUATION.

637
00:28:00,345 --> 00:28:02,881
Jay: YAYA.
EVA.

638
00:28:02,881 --> 00:28:05,918
Eva: I'M DEFINITELY NERVOUS,
BECAUSE I KNOW WHAT ALL

639
00:28:05,918 --> 00:28:07,653
IS RIDING ON THIS.

640
00:28:07,653 --> 00:28:09,721
AND IT'S LIKE, WHOA,
THIS IS IT.

641
00:28:09,721 --> 00:28:10,722
DON'T MESS UP.

642
00:28:10,722 --> 00:28:12,257
Tyra: ARE YOU READY?
Eva: YES.

643
00:28:12,257 --> 00:28:13,926
Tyra: ARE YOU NERVOUS?
Eva: YES.

644
00:28:13,926 --> 00:28:15,861
Tyra: I'M NERVOUS, TOO.

645
00:28:15,861 --> 00:28:18,630
YOU GUYS ARE WITH REAL MODELS
TODAY, SO YOU HAVE TO STEP UP.

646
00:28:18,630 --> 00:28:21,033
THEY'VE BEEN DOING THIS
FOR A LOT LONGER THAN YOU HAVE.

647
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:23,235
AND THEY'RE PROBABLY
LOOKIN' AT YOU, LIKE...

648
00:28:23,235 --> 00:28:25,170
SO YOU GOTTA
SERVE IT RIGHT BACK.

649
00:28:25,170 --> 00:28:27,139
Yaya: MY HEART WAS BEATING
FAST, AND I JUST HAD TO,

650
00:28:27,139 --> 00:28:28,674
LIKE, REFOCUS AND RECENTER.

651
00:28:28,674 --> 00:28:31,143
AND THIS IS JUST IT.

652
00:28:31,143 --> 00:28:32,978
Tyra: ALL RIGHT.

653
00:28:32,978 --> 00:28:34,213
Jay: OKAY, THIS IS JAY.

654
00:28:34,213 --> 00:28:37,883
WE ARE GOING TO
START THE SHOW NOW.

655
00:28:45,924 --> 00:28:47,893
Jay: I'M SENDING OUT
THE TAIKO DRUMMERS.

656
00:28:47,893 --> 00:28:51,563
WE ARE GOING TO
START THE SHOW NOW.

657
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:54,866
(drums play)

658
00:28:58,203 --> 00:29:00,405
Eva: THIS IS
THE FINAL COMPETITION,

659
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:04,876
THE FINAL CHALLENGE
IN DETERMINING WHO WINS.

660
00:29:04,876 --> 00:29:07,379
Yaya: THE DRUMS
JUST MADE MY HEART BEAT FASTER,

661
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:09,014
MADE ME SO MUCH MORE NERVOUS.

662
00:29:16,922 --> 00:29:17,923
Both: HA!

663
00:29:17,923 --> 00:29:18,924
Jay: GO!

664
00:29:18,924 --> 00:29:22,661
♪♪♪

665
00:29:22,661 --> 00:29:25,030
Jay: OKAY, YAYA, GO.

666
00:29:25,030 --> 00:29:26,365
Janice: YEAH!

667
00:29:26,365 --> 00:29:28,200
Yaya: WALKING OUT
ONTO THE RUNWAY AND NOT BEING

668
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:30,502
ABLE TO LOOK AT THE PEOPLE,
BUT JUST FEELING THEM

669
00:29:30,502 --> 00:29:34,539
WATCHING ME IS EXHILARATING.

670
00:29:34,539 --> 00:29:38,510
Eva: I LIKE TO WALK STRONG
AND JUST SERVE IT.

671
00:29:38,510 --> 00:29:42,347
BUT THIS FASHION SHOW
DIDN'T ALLOW ME TO DO THAT.

672
00:29:42,347 --> 00:29:44,583
BACKSTAGE IS CRAZY.

673
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:46,285
EVERYONE'S GETTING DRESSED.

674
00:29:46,285 --> 00:29:47,352
PEOPLE ARE YELLING
AND SCREAMING.

675
00:29:47,352 --> 00:29:48,353
Jay: I NEED MORE GIRLS!

676
00:29:48,353 --> 00:29:49,655
MORE GIRLS!

677
00:29:49,655 --> 00:29:51,590
Eva: IT'S MADNESS BACKSTAGE.

678
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:54,960
Yaya: AS SOON AS I GOT
MY CLOTHES ON, IT WAS MY TURN.

679
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:56,495
Jay: OKAY, I NEED YOU NOW,
RIGHT NOW.

680
00:29:56,495 --> 00:29:57,663
GO.

681
00:30:04,303 --> 00:30:06,204
Janice: YAYA!

682
00:30:06,204 --> 00:30:07,506
FASTER!

683
00:30:07,506 --> 00:30:08,940
Jay: OKAY, I NEED YOU NOW,
RIGHT NOW.

684
00:30:15,547 --> 00:30:16,915
Janice: OH, THAT'S PERFECT.

685
00:30:22,954 --> 00:30:24,956
Eva: I LOOK AT MY RACK
AND IT'S MY LAST OUTFIT.

686
00:30:24,956 --> 00:30:26,958
Jay: THIS IS YOUR
LAST OUTFIT, GIRLS.

687
00:30:26,958 --> 00:30:28,060
Eva: THIS IS MY LAST
OPPORTUNITY TO SHOW THEM

688
00:30:28,060 --> 00:30:29,261
THAT I AM WORTHY.

689
00:30:29,261 --> 00:30:30,962
Jay: BLAH, BLAH, BLAH.
LET'S GET YOU FIRST.

690
00:30:30,962 --> 00:30:31,997
FIRST, FIRST, FIRST.

691
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:33,632
OKAY, YOU TWO,
YAYA, NOW.

692
00:30:36,134 --> 00:30:37,402
Janice: LOVE THAT.

693
00:30:37,402 --> 00:30:38,570
Yaya: EVERY TIME
I EXIT THE STAGE,

694
00:30:38,570 --> 00:30:40,072
EVA CROSSES IN FRONT OF ME.

695
00:30:40,072 --> 00:30:43,942
THE RULE IS LET THE PERSON
WHO'S ENTERING GO FIRST.

696
00:30:43,942 --> 00:30:45,944
I WAS WAITING FOR HER
TO GO, GO, GO, GO.

697
00:30:45,944 --> 00:30:48,313
I REALLY HAD TO SLOW DOWN.

698
00:30:48,313 --> 00:30:49,581
Eva: THERE COULD HAVE
DEFINITELY BEEN A HUGE

699
00:30:49,581 --> 00:30:51,416
CRASH COLLISION THERE.

700
00:30:51,416 --> 00:30:55,587
♪♪♪

701
00:31:01,326 --> 00:31:04,529
(cheers and applause)

702
00:31:14,439 --> 00:31:18,276
Yaya: THE SHOW WAS OVER,
AND IT'S OUR LAST CHALLENGE.

703
00:31:18,276 --> 00:31:20,545
I FEEL REALLY GOOD
ABOUT MY PERFORMANCE.

704
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:23,949
SO MY CHANCES OF WINNING
ARE VERY GOOD.

705
00:31:23,949 --> 00:31:26,184
Eva: I FEEL GREAT.
I FEEL LIKE I WAS ON POINT.

706
00:31:26,184 --> 00:31:27,953
I FEEL LIKE I DID
A REALLY GOOD JOB.

707
00:31:27,953 --> 00:31:29,554
Jay: YOU GUYS
WALKED AT THE RIGHT PACE.

708
00:31:29,554 --> 00:31:31,390
YOU GUYS WERE DEAD ON.

709
00:31:31,390 --> 00:31:33,959
SO NOW THE TWO OF YOU GUYS
ARE GONNA GO TO JUDGING...

710
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:35,527
Eva: ALL RIGHT.
Jay: FROM HERE.

711
00:31:35,527 --> 00:31:37,462
Yaya: RIGHT NOW.
Jay: RIGHT NOW.

712
00:31:37,462 --> 00:31:39,498
Yaya: IT'S JUST
FROM THE FASHION SHOW

713
00:31:39,498 --> 00:31:40,966
STRAIGHT TO PANEL.

714
00:31:40,966 --> 00:31:42,934
EVA KIND OF COLLAPSED
INTO MY BOSOM.

715
00:31:42,934 --> 00:31:44,536
SHE'S MY COMPETITOR,
BUT AT THAT MOMENT, I FELT LIKE,

716
00:31:44,536 --> 00:31:46,571
"ALL RIGHT, HERE WE GO."

717
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:49,374
Eva: THIS WHOLE
COMPETITION STUFF IS OVER.

718
00:31:49,374 --> 00:31:52,644
IT'S TIME TO GO TO PANEL,
AND ONE GIRL IS ABOUT TO BECOME

719
00:31:52,644 --> 00:31:54,112
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

720
00:31:59,484 --> 00:32:02,020
Tyra: BEAUTIFUL.

721
00:32:02,020 --> 00:32:03,622
WELL, YOU GUYS, THIS IS IT.

722
00:32:03,622 --> 00:32:09,261
WE'VE WATCHED BOTH OF YOU
TRANSFORM FROM LITTLE GIRL

723
00:32:09,261 --> 00:32:11,496
FROM NEW YORK,
LITTLE GIRL FROM L.A.,

724
00:32:11,496 --> 00:32:15,567
INTO BEAUTIFUL,
WORLD-CLASS MODELS.

725
00:32:15,567 --> 00:32:19,971
BUT ONLY ONE OF YOU CAN BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

726
00:32:19,971 --> 00:32:22,207
THE WINNER TONIGHT
IS GETTIN' SOME AMAZING PRIZES.

727
00:32:22,207 --> 00:32:23,575
Both: MM-HMM.

728
00:32:23,575 --> 00:32:26,912
Tyra: THE FIRST IS A BIG,
FAT CONTRACT WITH THE TOP

729
00:32:26,912 --> 00:32:30,482
INTERNATIONAL MODELING AGENCY
FORD MODELS.

730
00:32:30,482 --> 00:32:33,418
THE WINNER WILL BE SHOT BY
WORLD-RENOWNED PHOTOGRAPHER

731
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:36,388
GILLES BENSIMON
IN A PHOTO SPREAD

732
00:32:36,388 --> 00:32:39,057
FOR "ELLE" MAGAZINE.

733
00:32:39,057 --> 00:32:43,395
AND LAST BUT NOT LEAST,
A $100,000 CONTRACT

734
00:32:43,395 --> 00:32:46,331
FOR COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

735
00:32:46,331 --> 00:32:49,901
NOW, OF COURSE, OUR JUDGES--
JANICE DICKINSON, ONE OF

736
00:32:49,901 --> 00:32:52,337
THE WORLD'S FIRST SUPERMODELS.

737
00:32:52,337 --> 00:32:55,140
NIGEL BARKER,
A NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER.

738
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:58,143
NOLé MARIN, PROMINENT
FASHION EDITOR AND STYLIST.

739
00:32:58,143 --> 00:32:59,311
AND THAT'S IT TONIGHT.

740
00:32:59,311 --> 00:33:03,381
AS YOU GUYS CAN SEE,
THERE IS NO GUEST JUDGE.

741
00:33:03,381 --> 00:33:06,885
THAT'S BECAUSE WE KNOW YOU BEST.

742
00:33:06,885 --> 00:33:10,255
WE KNOW YOUR STRENGTHS,
AND WE KNOW YOUR WEAKNESSES.

743
00:33:10,255 --> 00:33:12,958
SO NOW IT'S TIME
FOR YOUR EVALUATIONS.

744
00:33:12,958 --> 00:33:15,126
AND THEN AFTER THAT,
THE JUDGES WILL DELIBERATE

745
00:33:15,126 --> 00:33:18,897
AND WILL DETERMINE
WHICH ONE OF YOU WILL BECOME

746
00:33:18,897 --> 00:33:20,198
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

747
00:33:20,198 --> 00:33:22,434
Eva: (sighs)
Yaya: OH, MY GOD.

748
00:33:22,434 --> 00:33:24,369
Tyra: BOTH OF YOU WALKED IN
A VERY IMPORTANT FASHION SHOW

749
00:33:24,369 --> 00:33:26,338
FOR DESIGNER NORIKO FUKUSHIMA.

750
00:33:26,338 --> 00:33:30,242
NOW LET'S TAKE A LOOK
AT YOUR FOOTAGE.

751
00:33:30,242 --> 00:33:32,511
Nigel: YAYA, WHEN YOU WALKED
OUT ONTO THAT RUNWAY,

752
00:33:32,511 --> 00:33:34,112
I WAS BREATHLESS.

753
00:33:34,112 --> 00:33:35,347
YOU LOOKED BEAUTIFUL.

754
00:33:35,347 --> 00:33:36,515
Nolé: YOU WERE SO TECHNICAL.

755
00:33:36,515 --> 00:33:38,316
IT WAS ACTUALLY VERY IMPRESSIVE.

756
00:33:38,316 --> 00:33:41,486
BUT I FELT THAT IT LACKED
A LITTLE BIT OF A PERSONALITY.

757
00:33:41,486 --> 00:33:43,588
Janice: YAYA,
YOU FIT RIGHT IN.

758
00:33:43,588 --> 00:33:46,558
BUT THE LOOK ON YOUR FACE
WAS THAT OF A ZOMBIE.

759
00:33:46,558 --> 00:33:48,159
IT WAS GLACIAL.

760
00:33:48,159 --> 00:33:50,328
I THINK YOU'LL GET IT
THE NEXT TIME

761
00:33:50,328 --> 00:33:51,463
YOU HAVE A FASHION SHOW.

762
00:33:51,463 --> 00:33:53,098
Tyra: MY MAMA MADE A COMMENT.

763
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:54,533
SHE WAS LIKE,
"LOOK AT HER BOOTY.

764
00:33:54,533 --> 00:33:57,002
OH, SHE'S GOT A GREAT BODY."

765
00:33:57,002 --> 00:33:58,870
Nigel: EVA,
I REALLY LIKED YOUR WALK.

766
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,372
YOU HAD THE ZEN,
STILL THAT LITTLE BIT

767
00:34:00,372 --> 00:34:02,941
OF EVA SORT OF SWAGGER TO IT.

768
00:34:02,941 --> 00:34:05,176
Tyra: ONE THING THAT I
NOTICED THAT YOU DO,

769
00:34:05,176 --> 00:34:08,513
ESPECIALLY ON THE PROFILE,
IS YOU DO THIS.

770
00:34:08,513 --> 00:34:10,014
Janice: A LITTLE EGRET.

771
00:34:10,014 --> 00:34:12,217
Tyra: IT WAS, LIKE,
PROPELLING YOU FORWARD.

772
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:15,152
YAYA, YOU WERE DOING
TOO MUCH HEEL-TOE.

773
00:34:15,152 --> 00:34:18,255
YOU HAVE TO PUT THAT PRESSURE
MORE ON THE BALLS TO MAKE IT

774
00:34:18,255 --> 00:34:20,559
A LITTLE BIT MORE ELEGANT.

775
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:22,627
YOU'VE BEEN HERE FOR 12 WEEKS.

776
00:34:22,627 --> 00:34:25,630
AND YOU'VE TAKEN
SOME BEAUTIFUL PICTURES.

777
00:34:25,630 --> 00:34:28,967
HERE'S YOUR FIRST WEEK HERE.

778
00:34:28,967 --> 00:34:30,435
SEEMS LIKE A LONG TIME AGO.

779
00:34:30,435 --> 00:34:32,504
Nigel: I THINK THIS WAS WHEN
I FIRST NOTICED YOU, YAYA.

780
00:34:32,504 --> 00:34:36,241
YOU NAILED THIS LOOK, I THINK,
BETTER THAN ANY OF THE GIRLS.

781
00:34:36,241 --> 00:34:37,442
Janice: EVA, YOU'VE GOT IT
IN THE EYES BUT EVERYTHING ELSE

782
00:34:37,442 --> 00:34:39,210
IS COLLAPSED.

783
00:34:39,210 --> 00:34:40,911
Tyra: EVA,
YOURS IS A LITTLE COMMON.

784
00:34:40,911 --> 00:34:43,081
YOU WEREN'T SUPER COMFORTABLE
MODELING YET.

785
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:46,251
SO YOU WENT TO THE COMFY,
JUST CHILLIN' OUT POSE.

786
00:34:46,251 --> 00:34:48,085
Janice: THAT'S LIKE A POSE
THAT WE ALL DO

787
00:34:48,085 --> 00:34:49,420
IN THE FIFTH OR SIXTH GRADE.

788
00:34:49,420 --> 00:34:52,123
Tyra: HEY!
Janice: IN THE SCHOOLYARD--HI.

789
00:34:52,123 --> 00:34:54,626
Nolé: THEY BOTH ARE JUST
INCREDIBLE, INCREDIBLE SHOTS.

790
00:34:54,626 --> 00:34:56,895
Nigel: I THINK YOU BOTH
STEPPED IT UP A NOTCH HERE.

791
00:34:56,895 --> 00:34:58,630
Nolé: EVA, THIS IS WHEN
I REALLY STARTED TAKING NOTICE

792
00:34:58,630 --> 00:35:00,565
OF YOU AS A BEAUTY GIRL.

793
00:35:00,565 --> 00:35:02,200
Nigel: YAYA, FOR ME, IT WAS
OBVIOUS THAT YOU WERE BEAUTIFUL

794
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:04,002
STRAIGHT AWAY.

795
00:35:04,002 --> 00:35:05,570
IN THIS PICTURE,
YOU NAILED IT.

796
00:35:05,570 --> 00:35:07,606
Tyra: THIS WAS
YOUR ALTER EGO WEEK.

797
00:35:07,606 --> 00:35:09,374
Janice: EVA, GORGEOUS.

798
00:35:09,374 --> 00:35:11,409
DROP-DEAD KNOCKOUT PILL
BETTY GRABLE, RITA HAYWORTH,

799
00:35:11,409 --> 00:35:13,645
JUST GORGEOUS.

800
00:35:13,645 --> 00:35:14,546
Nolé: THIS
IS WHEN THE COMPETITION

801
00:35:14,546 --> 00:35:16,047
REALLY GOT TOUGH.

802
00:35:16,047 --> 00:35:18,617
EVA, YOU NAILED THIS SHOT
IN BOTH.

803
00:35:18,617 --> 00:35:20,885
YAYA, THE ONE SHOT,
WHEN YOU'RE ON THE CAR,

804
00:35:20,885 --> 00:35:24,556
IS VERY COUTURE,
BUT I DON'T LIKE

805
00:35:24,556 --> 00:35:26,157
THE NATURAL SHOT.

806
00:35:26,157 --> 00:35:28,994
IT DOESN'T SAY ENOUGH.

807
00:35:28,994 --> 00:35:30,195
Tyra: THAT'S CRAZY.

808
00:35:30,195 --> 00:35:31,196
YAYA'S PICTURE CAME UP,
AND I WAS LIKE,

809
00:35:31,196 --> 00:35:33,098
"WHAT'S MY PICTURE
DOIN' UP THERE?"

810
00:35:33,098 --> 00:35:37,402
Nolé: EVA, YOU WERE THE ONE
WHO WAS PETRIFIED OF THE SPIDER.

811
00:35:37,402 --> 00:35:41,106
BUT IN THE PASSION OF YOUR EYES,
I DON'T SEE IT AT ALL.

812
00:35:41,106 --> 00:35:42,507
Nigel: YAYA, FOR ME,
IT'S THE MOST UNBELIEVABLE SHOT

813
00:35:42,507 --> 00:35:44,643
I'VE SEEN OF YOU.

814
00:35:44,643 --> 00:35:46,244
I THINK IT'S THE BEST SHOT
YOU'VE TAKEN SO FAR.

815
00:35:46,244 --> 00:35:48,546
GORGEOUS PICTURE.

816
00:35:48,546 --> 00:35:51,549
Tyra: I DID A LITTLE DEMO
FOR YOU WITH THIS SHOOT.

817
00:35:51,549 --> 00:35:54,386
I WAS VERY IMPRESSED WITH YAYA,
BECAUSE YOU WERE TAKING NOTES

818
00:35:54,386 --> 00:35:56,454
IN YOUR HEAD WHEN I WAS POSING.

819
00:35:56,454 --> 00:35:59,524
Nolé: EVA, I MUST SAY
THAT I LIKE YOUR BODY LANGUAGE

820
00:35:59,524 --> 00:36:01,259
IN THIS SHOT.

821
00:36:01,259 --> 00:36:02,394
Nigel: YOU TOOK ADVANTAGE
OF THE FACT THAT YOU'RE

822
00:36:02,394 --> 00:36:05,964
NOT PARTICULARLY TALL,
AND YOU ANGLED YOUR LEG NICELY.

823
00:36:05,964 --> 00:36:10,435
Janice: OH, EVA DIVA,
THIS IS EVA DIVA EXTRAORDINAIRE.

824
00:36:10,435 --> 00:36:12,504
GIRL, YOU'RE SLAMMIN'
IN THIS PHOTOGRAPH.

825
00:36:12,504 --> 00:36:14,906
Nigel: YAYA, THERE'S
NO ARROGANCE IN THIS PICTURE.

826
00:36:14,906 --> 00:36:16,474
YOU'RE JUST VERY APPROACHABLE.

827
00:36:16,474 --> 00:36:20,178
Nolé: EVA WAS SO FRIENDLY.
IT'S SO WARM AND INVITING.

828
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:22,347
Tyra: I KNOW COVER GIRL'S
MOTTO IS LIKE A GOOD GIRL

829
00:36:22,347 --> 00:36:23,515
WITH A WINK.

830
00:36:23,515 --> 00:36:25,884
AND I THINK
BOTH OF YOU HAVE THAT.

831
00:36:25,884 --> 00:36:28,319
AND I THINK BOTH OF YOU WOULD
MAKE A REALLY GREAT COVER GIRL.

832
00:36:28,319 --> 00:36:30,088
Janice: WINNING LOOKS.
Tyra: YEAH.

833
00:36:30,088 --> 00:36:33,324
SO NOW IT IS TIME
TO DELIBERATE.

834
00:36:33,324 --> 00:36:37,662
AND WHEN I CALL YOU BACK,
I WILL ANNOUNCE WHO WILL BECOME

835
00:36:37,662 --> 00:36:39,664
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

836
00:36:42,434 --> 00:36:44,302
Nigel: BOTH YAYA AND EVA
ARE STRIKING IN DIFFERENT WAYS.

837
00:36:44,302 --> 00:36:48,106
EVA HAS AN UNUSUAL LOOK
THAT I SEE MORE OF RIGHT NOW.

838
00:36:48,106 --> 00:36:50,108
YAYA HAS A VERY OLD-FASHIONED
LOOK FOR ME.

839
00:36:50,108 --> 00:36:52,410
AND SO IT'S NOT THAT I PREFER
ONE OVER THE OTHER,

840
00:36:52,410 --> 00:36:54,612
I'M SORT OF GOING
BACK AND FORTH.

841
00:36:54,612 --> 00:36:56,614
Tyra: INTERESTING
THAT YAYA DOESN'T HAVE

842
00:36:56,614 --> 00:37:00,618
MODELING EXPERIENCE,
BUT VERY EARLY ON WAS MOVING

843
00:37:00,618 --> 00:37:02,120
KIND OF LIKE A PRO.

844
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:05,657
Nolé: TODAY, I ALMOST
FELL DOWN WHEN I SAW

845
00:37:05,657 --> 00:37:08,960
HOW INCREDIBLE EVA LOOKED.

846
00:37:08,960 --> 00:37:11,096
SHE LOOKED LIKE A SUPERSTAR.

847
00:37:11,096 --> 00:37:12,931
Janice: I SEE A BEAUTIFUL
WOMAN IN EVA.

848
00:37:12,931 --> 00:37:15,934
I SEE, YES,
SHE'S GROWN INCREDIBLY.

849
00:37:15,934 --> 00:37:19,170
BUT I'M MORE PRONE
TO YAYA'S REFINEMENT.

850
00:37:19,170 --> 00:37:22,440
I WATCH BOTH OF THE GIRLS
PAINSTAKINGLY

851
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:26,211
IN THE FASHION SHOW, AND YAYA
IS THE MORE VERSATILE MODEL.

852
00:37:26,211 --> 00:37:28,012
Nolé: EVA NEEDS TO UNDERSTAND
WHO SHE IS A LITTLE BIT MORE

853
00:37:28,012 --> 00:37:29,180
AS A MODEL.

854
00:37:29,180 --> 00:37:30,448
Nigel: I FIND HER AMUSING.

855
00:37:30,448 --> 00:37:32,250
SHE MAKES ME SMILE
WHEN SHE'S IN FRONT OF ME.

856
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:35,153
AND IT'S NOT SOMETHING THAT YOU
CAN REALLY LEARN THAT EASILY.

857
00:37:35,153 --> 00:37:37,088
YOU EITHER HAVE THAT
OR YOU DON'T.

858
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:38,490
Janice: WELL,
THEY BOTH HAVE IT.

859
00:37:38,490 --> 00:37:39,958
Nigel: THEY BOTH HAVE IT, BUT--
Janice: THEY BOTH HAVE IT.

860
00:37:39,958 --> 00:37:41,159
THEY'RE JUST DIFFERENT
IN WHAT YOU PREFER.

861
00:37:41,159 --> 00:37:46,030
Tyra: YAYA--HER BODY
IS CRAZY, AMAZING.

862
00:37:46,030 --> 00:37:48,099
BODIES LIKE THIS
DON'T COME AROUND OFTEN.

863
00:37:48,099 --> 00:37:50,602
Nolé: BUT EVA--
SHE'S LIKE A CINDERELLA.

864
00:37:50,602 --> 00:37:52,604
SHE COMES IN LIKE A LITTLE
TOUGH BOY, AND SHE TURNED

865
00:37:52,604 --> 00:37:55,406
INTO THIS INCREDIBLY GORGEOUS,
BEAUTIFUL WOMAN.

866
00:37:55,406 --> 00:37:57,642
Nigel: I'M VERY TORN,
BECAUSE I HAVE INSTINCTS

867
00:37:57,642 --> 00:37:59,444
WHICH SAY YAYA,

868
00:37:59,444 --> 00:38:01,546
BUT THEN I HAVE ANOTHER SIDE
OF ME WHICH SAYS EVA.

869
00:38:01,546 --> 00:38:03,715
Tyra: THIS IS HORRIBLE.

870
00:38:12,157 --> 00:38:14,092
Tyra: IN A MOMENT,
I'M GOING TO ANNOUNCE

871
00:38:14,092 --> 00:38:16,461
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

872
00:38:16,461 --> 00:38:18,596
YOU GUYS HAVE HAD
QUITE A JOURNEY.

